WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:00.900
Hi.

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.000
My name is Michal Gala.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.170
And I am a junior in
chemical engineering,

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.260
doing research in
[INAUDIBLE] theorem group

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.840
on electrochemical
ammonia production.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.840
The reason for this is
important because ammonia

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.000
goes into all agricultural
production in the world in the

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.250
from of fertilizer.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:19.130
It has fueled the steady
growth of a world population

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:20.700
over the last 100 years.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.300
But the method we currently
have available of producing

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.730
it has a very large
capital cost, upwards

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.010
of a billion dollars
per a single plant,

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.560
and carries a proportional
penalty, in terms of,

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.670
CO2 emissions.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.910
This is why we are
trying to utilize

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:39.620
lithium's natural reactivity
towards gaseous nitrogen

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.950
to produce ammonia at ambient
temperature and pressure

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:46.940
with oxygen as the only
byproduct of a reaction.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:50.420
We do so by producing lithium
nitride from metallic lithium

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.850
and nitrogen, and
then hydrolyzing

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:55.670
this compound forming ammonia,
which has been released

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:58.850
and quantified, and
lithium ions, which

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:01.940
are then electrochemically
re-plated as lithium metal.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:05.209
This process requires a hydrogen
carrier, so a product source.

00:01:05.209 --> 00:01:07.203
And this is where
my project comes in.

00:01:07.203 --> 00:01:08.870
I am looking at
different compounds that

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:10.520
can be used for that
purpose and trying

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:12.680
to find trends between them.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.853
We identified three
groups of compounds.

00:01:14.853 --> 00:01:17.270
Some of them are active in the
process and produce ammonia

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:21.260
as is expected and reported
in previous literature.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:23.070
But some of them do not do that.

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:24.770
We divided them
into two categories

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:27.160
for inactive and the
hyperactive sources.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.720
Inactive sources,
in some way, do not

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.660
seem to activate
lithium towards reaction

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.630
with nitrogen, so the
nitridation reaction,

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:39.820
and do not give any yield
of ammonia produced.

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:41.720
And we are now doing
research trying

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:43.730
to explain why that
is because it's

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:45.710
a very surprising
result because lithium

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:47.360
reacts with nitrogen by itself.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:51.470
It shouldn't need to be
activated towards that.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:52.910
Another interesting
result we got

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:56.530
is the specific characteristics
of an active [INAUDIBLE]

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:57.790
sources.

00:01:57.790 --> 00:01:59.480
And it turns out
that some of them

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:02.900
are not exactly the same as
reported literature, which

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:06.020
means that very small structural
changes to the molecules

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:10.490
cause a big difference in
their reactivity in the system.

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:13.670
Doing that allowed us to
optimize the ammonia production

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:17.180
as a function of concentration
and choice of [INAUDIBLE]

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:19.850
source leading to
significant improvements

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:24.120
in faradaic efficiencies
of produced ammonia using,

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.810
especially, [INAUDIBLE] source.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.570
Thank you.

